<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pánfilo de Narváez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1478–1528</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pánfilo de Narváez was a Spanish conquistador who took part in the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>. In 1520 the governor of Cuba sent him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> with a large force to arrest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a>, but Cortés surprised him at Cempoala, captured him and won over most of his men. In 1527 he led an expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> that ended in disaster; he was lost at sea in 1528, and only four men, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvar-nunez-cabeza-de-vaca">Cabeza de Vaca</a>, survived.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/panfilo-de-narvaez.jpg" alt="Pánfilo de Narváez" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: historicair 14:56, 31 August 2007 (UTC) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panfilo_de_Narvaez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
